.00, q4 200.00, ratio 2500, len 260/350\n12. \"DN100-TU1M25-3150\": DN100, WE100, TU1M25 DN25, q1 0.051, q2 0.081, ratio 3150, len 260/350\n13. \"DN100-TU1M25-4000\": DN100, WE100, TU1M25 DN25, q1 0.04, q2 0.064, ratio 4000, len 260/350\n14. \"DN100-TU1M25-5000\": DN100, WE100, TU1M25 DN25, q1 0.032, q2 0.051, ratio 5000, len 260/350\n15. \"DN100-AquadisP111-8000\": DN100, WE100, Aquadis+ P111 DN25, q1 0.02, q2 0.032, ratio 8000, len 260/350\n16. \"DN150-TU1M25-6300\": DN150, WE150, TU1M25 DN25, q1 0.063, q2 0.102, q3 400.00, q4 500.00, ratio 6300, len 260/500\n17. \"DN150-TU1M25-8000\": DN150, WE150, TU1M25 DN25, q1 0.05, q2 0.08, ratio 8000, len 260/500\n18. \"DN150-TU1M25-10000\": DN150, WE150, TU1M25 DN25, q1 0.04, q2 0.064, ratio 10000, len 260/500\n19. \"DN150-TU1M25-12500\": DN150, WE150, TU1M25 DN25, q1 0.032, q2 0.051, ratio 12500, len 260/500\n20. \"DN150-TU140F-4000\": DN150, WE150, TU1 40F DN40, q1 0.1, q2 0.16, ratio 4000, len 260/500\n21. \"DN150-P290plus-4000\": DN150, WE150, P290+ DN40, q1 0.1, q2 0.16, ratio 4000, len 300/500\n22. \"DN150-P290plus-8000\": DN150, WE150, P290+ DN40, q1 0.05, q2 0.08, ratio 8000, len 300/500\n\nGood.\n\nGiven the size, I'm going to also keep matrix_tables rows complete-ish since they're the authoritative preservation. Each table gets a \"variants\" column with model_id, plus primary/secondary/q values/lengths/resolution_secondary, and for table 4 indicating range secondary.\n\nLet me think about total size again... It'll be long but let's go. Actually, to control length, I'll make matrix_tables rows minimal but complete on per-column data, and put table-level constants in `description`.\n\nNow type_level characteristics:\n\n{\n  \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n  \"temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"T30\", ...},\n  \"maximum_admissible_temperature\": {\"value\": 30, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n  \"maximum_admissible_pressure\": {\"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"},\n  \"orientation_limitation\": {\"value\": \"H\"},\n  \"installation_orientation\": {\"value\": \"H\"},\n  \"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"mechanical water meter\"},\n  \"eut_testing_category\": {\"value\": \"Positive displacement meters and turbine water meters\"},\n  \"eut_testing_case\": {\"value\": \"A\"},\n  \"changeover_zone_definition\": {\"value\": \"Qmin(main) < Zc < 1.2 × Qn(secondary)\"}\n}\n\nenvironmental_class and electromagnetic environment are \"-\" — omit (not meaningful values). Mounting \"-\" omit.\n\nRecommendation scheme: \"B\".\n\nCertificate number: \"R49/2013-CZ-16.02\". Note it's \"R49/2013-CZ-16.02\" — include as-is.\n\nIssuing authority address: \"Okružní 31,\" and \"638 00 Brno, CZ\". I'll write address_lines: [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"]? The doc says CZ. Keep \"CZ\" as in doc: [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"CZ\"]. Fine.\n\nApplicant address: \"11 bvd Pasteur 67500 Haguenau France\" → [\"11 bvd Pasteur\", \"67500 Haguenau\", \"France\"].\n\noiml_issuer_id: not given. Omit.\n\ndate_issued: \"2016-05-26\".\n\nproject_number: not given — omit.\n\nComponents:\n1. primary meter: role \"primary_meter\", type_designations [\"Woltex (WE50)\", \"Woltex (WE65)\", \"Woltex (WE100)\", \"Woltex (WE150)\"], characteristics: {\"meter_type\": {\"value\": \"Woltman meter\"}, \"register\": {\"value\": \"mechanical dry-dial\"}}\n2. secondary meter: role \"secondary_meter\", type_designations [\"TU1M20 DN20\", \"TU1M25 DN25\", \"TU1 40F DN40\", \"Aquadis+ P1 DN20\", \"Aquadis+ P111 DN25\", \"P290+ DN40\"], characteristics: {\"meter_type\": {\"value\": \"single jet or rotary piston meter\"}, \"register\": {\"value\": \"mechanical dry-dial\"}}\n3. changeover valve: role \"changeover_valve\", type_designations: [] — hmm empty array; maybe omit characteristics.\n4. indicating devices: role \"indicating_device\", type_designations [], characteristics {\"count\": 2, \"type\": \"mechanical dry dial with pointers and rollers\"} — maybe skip this one; the two indicating devices are part of primary/secondary meters. I'll include it as it's described (\"equipped with two indicating devices\"). Eh — keep components to the three named devices; describing indicators via type_level. I'll include a components entry for indicating devices since the description explicitly covers them. Let me include it.\n\ncharacteristics within components use the structured {value, unit_symbol, unit_id} shape. OK.\n\nNow write the final JSON. Be careful: no LaTeX, snake_case labels, structured values.\n\nFor model_level value objects, include \"footnote_markers\" only when applicable (none here). I'll omit empty footnote_markers.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-CZ-16.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"B\",\n    \"page_total\": 7,\n    \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2016-05-26\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Czech Metrology Institute\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"CZ\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Jan Kalandra\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\"name\": \"Itron\", \"address_lines\": [\"11 bvd Pasteur\", \"67500 Haguenau\", \"France\"]}\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\"name\": \"Itron\", \"address_lines\": [\"11 bvd Pasteur\", \"67500 Haguenau\", \"France\"]}\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"ISOFLO\", \"Woltex (WE)\", \"TU1M20\", \"TU1M25\", \"TU1 40F\", \"Aquadis+\", \"Aquadis+ P1\", \"Aquadis+ P111\", \"P290+\"],\n    \"module_designation\": null,\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"ISOFLO\",\n    \"models\": [ ...22 entries... ]\n  },\n  \"components\": [ ... ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": { ... },\n    \"model_level\": [ ...8 entries... ],\n    \"config_level\": [ ...9 entries... ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [ ...4... ],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49\",\n    \"edition\": 2013,\n    \"scheme\": \"B\",\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [2]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [\n    {\"id\": \"6015-PT-P007-16\", \"pages\": 42, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nDescription text: \"Combination water meter for cold potable water, mechanical principle. Comprises primary (main) Woltman meter Woltex (WE), secondary (by-pass) meter (single jet TU1M20/TU1M25/TU1 40F or rotary piston Aquadis+ P1/P111/P290+), changeover valve and two mechanical dry-dial indicating devices (pointers and rollers). Displays volume in m³ and flow rate in m³/h. Not designed to measure reverse flow. Intended for horizontal pipework with indicating device on top. Changeover zone: Qmin(main) < Zc < 1.2×Qn(secondary). Markings: unit of measurement (m³), Q3 value and Q3/Q1 ratio, OIML certificate number, manufacturer name/trademark, year of manufacture, serial number, flow direction arrow, MAP, letter H, temperature class T30, pressure loss class, installation sensitivity class.\"\n\nNow model_level arrays. Let me write them fully.\n\nnominal_diameter values:\nDN50-TU1M20-1600: 50\nDN50-AquadisP1-2500: 50\nDN50-AquadisP1-4000: 50\nDN65-TU1M20-4000: 65\nDN65-AquadisP1-4000: 65\nDN65-AquadisP1-6300: 65\nDN80-TU1M20-6300: 80\nDN80-AquadisP1-10000: 80\nDN80-AquadisP1-16000: 80\nDN100-TU1M20-6300: 100\nDN100-TU1M25-2500: 100\nDN100-TU1M25-3150: 100\nDN100-TU1M25-4000: 100\nDN100-TU1M25-5000: 100\nDN100-AquadisP111-8000: 100\nDN150-TU1M25-6300: 150\nDN150-TU1M25-8000: 150\nDN150-TU1M25-10000: 150\nDN150-TU1M25-12500: 150\nDN150-TU140F-4000: 150\nDN150-P290plus-4000: 150\nDN150-P290plus-8000: 150\n\nq1: 0.025, 0.016, 0.01, 0.016, 0.016, 0.01, 0.025, 0.016, 0.01, 0.025, 0.064, 0.051, 0.04, 0.032, 0.02, 0.063, 0.05, 0.04, 0.032, 0.1, 0.1, 0.05\n\nq2: 0.04, 0.026, 0.016, 0.025, 0.025, 0.016, 0.041, 0.026, 0.016, 0.041, 0.102, 0.081, 0.064, 0.051, 0.032, 0.102, 0.08, 0.064, 0.051, 0.16, 0.16, 0.08\n\nq3: 40 (×3), 63 (×3), 160 (×6), 400 (×7). Wait: DN50×3=40, DN65×3=63, DN80×3=160, DN100×6=160 → 160×9, DN150×7=400. So: 40,40,40,63,63,63,160,160,160,160,160,160,160,160,160,400,400,400,400,400,400,400.\n\nq4: 50,50,50,78.75,78.75,78.75,200×9,500×7.\n\nq3_over_q1: 1600,2500,4000,4000,4000,6300,6300,10000,16000,6300,2500,3150,4000,5000,8000,6300,8000,10000,12500,4000,4000,8000.\n\nlength_secondary_meter: 190,190,190,190,190,190,190,190,190,190,260,260,260,260,260,260,260,260,260,260,300,300.\n\nlength_combination_meter: 300,300,300,300,300,300,350,350,350,350,350,350,350,350,350,500,500,500,500,500,500,500.\n\nOK. This is a lot of JSON but let's write it.\n\nFor the matrix_tables, columns naming: [\"model_id\", \"nominal_diameter\", \"primary_meter\", \"secondary_meter\", \"q1\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\", \"q3_over_q1\", \"qx1\", \"qx2\", \"length_secondary_meter\", \"length_combination_meter\", \"resolution_secondary\"]. column_units: [null, \"mm\", null, null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"mm\", \"mm\", \"dm³\"].\n\nTable descriptions:\n- t1: \"Table 1 – Basic technical parameters, ISOFLO DN 50. Common: accuracy class 2, temperature class T30, pressure loss class 25, max admissible temperature 30 °C, max admissible pressure 16 MPa, orientation H, indicating range primary 999999 or 9999999 m³, indicating range secondary 99999 m³, resolution primary 0.2 or 2 dm³, connection flange DN50, flow profile sensitivity class U0S D0, EUT category 'Positive displacement meters and turbine water meters', case A.\"\n- t2: \"Table 2 – ISOFLO DN 65 and DN 80. Common: accuracy class 2, T30, pressure loss class 40, 30 °C, 16 MPa, orientation H, primary indicating range 999999 or 9999999 m³, secondary 99999 m³, primary resolution 0.2 or 2 dm³, U0S D0, case A. DN65: flange DN65; DN80: flange DN80.\"\n- t3: \"Table 3 – ISOFLO DN 100. Common: accuracy class 2, T30, pressure loss class 25, 30 °C, 16 MPa, orientation H, primary range 999999 or 9999999 m³, secondary 99999 m³, primary resolution 0.2 or 2 dm³, flange DN100, U0S D0, case A.\"\n- t4: \"Table 4 – ISOFLO DN 150. Common: accuracy class 2, T30, pressure loss class 25, 30 °C, 16 MPa, orientation H, primary indicating range 9999999 or 99999999 m³, primary resolution 2 or 20 dm³ (20 dm³ usable up to Q1 = 3.125 m³/h included), flange DN150, U5S D0, case A. Secondary indicating range 99999 m³ for TU1M25 DN25 and TU1 40F DN40, 999999 m³ for P290+ DN40.\"\n\nRows for tables — include qx1, qx2 per row (same within table). For table 4 also include indicating_range_secondary and resolution_secondary per row.\n\nFootnotes: none. revision_history: none.\n\nOne more check — \"page_total\": 7. Yes \"Page 1 of 7 pages\".\n\nThe signature date: 26 May 2016 → date_issued \"2016-05-26\".\n\nAlso \"Pavel Klenovský\" signed as OIML Issuing Authority — maybe add to issuing_authority as person_responsible? The doc has both Jan Kalandra (person responsible) and Pavel Klenovský (signatory). I'll keep Jan Kalandra as person_responsible and could add a note... there's no field. Leave it.\n\nDouble-check Q2 values Table 3 col1: Q1=0.025, Q2=0.041 — yes matches DN80 TU1M20 too (same meter config, but different DN/lengths). Right.\n\nCheck Table 4 col 5 (TU1 40F): Q1=0.100, Q2=0.160, ratio 4000. Yes.\n\nCheck Aquadis+ P111 naming: \"Aquadis+P111 DN25\" in table 3 — text on page 2 mentions \"Aquadis+\". I'll write \"Aquadis+ P111 DN25\".\n\nScheme B: \"OIML BASIC CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMITY\" — scheme \"B\". Yes.\n\nNow, accuracy_classes: [\"2\"]? The rec line: \"R 49, edition 2013, for accuracy class 2\". I'll use [2]. Hmm — could also be strings. [2] fine.\n\nEdition: 2013 (int). Good.\n\nLet me also consider: should models[].attributes include connection etc.? I've decided config_level covers it. Attributes: primary_meter, secondary_meter only. Good.\n\nWrite the JSON now, carefully, valid JSON. Watch out for the \"³\" characters — fine in JSON.\n\nModel labels:\n1. \"ISOFLO DN50: Woltex WE50 + TU1M20 DN20, Q3/Q1 = 1600\"\netc. Keep shorter: \"DN5